at files it under transport error a great deal.\"},{\"text\":\"A 429 refusal costs the platform almost nothing.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"When that cap is spent the gateway answers 429 at the edge — without waking the service behind it — so the refusal costs the platform almost nothing and costs a caller that files it under transport error a great deal.\"},{\"text\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds, and never against a connection.\"},{\"text\":\"Requests are counted over a fixed window of 60 seconds.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds, and never against a connection.\"},{\"text\":\"Requests are never counted against a connection.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds, and never against a connection.\"},{\"text\":\"Opening a second socket buys a caller nothing in terms of rate limit.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Opening a second socket therefore buys a caller nothing.\"},{\"text\":\"A client spread across eight worker processes is throttled at exactly the point one process would have been.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"A client spread across eight worker processes is throttled at exactly the point one process would have been — and pays for the extra file descriptors as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window, and a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 requests in the same window.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window, and a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A 429 refusal is not an outage.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"A refusal is not an outage, whatever the error class in a client library happens to call it.\"},{\"text\":\"A 429 refusal is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"It is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else, and waiting is the only correct answer.\"},{\"text\":\"Callers that retry at once are the largest single reason the cap exists.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Callers that retry at once are the largest single reason the cap is there at all.\"},{\"text\":\"The 429 refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\"},{\"text\":\"The Retry-After header value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\"},{\"text\":\"Waiting longer than the Retry-After header asks earns a caller no credit.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the 429 refusal is JSON.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the 429 refusal names the window the gateway counted in.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the 429 refusal names the cap.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"It names the cap and the tier as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the 429 refusal names the tier.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"It names the cap and the tier as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the 429 refusal is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused — nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\"},{\"text\":\"Nothing in the body of the 429 refusal is meant for the retry loop.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused — nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway computes the wait with information the caller does not have.\",\"line\":19,\"span\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway computes the wait on the 503 path as well.\",\"line\":19,\"span\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 200 response wants nothing.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 429 response wants the stated wait.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 500 response may be retried once the stated wait has passed.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 503 response is the overload path.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A client that folds every non-success response into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\"},{\"text\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A batch credential is measured over exactly the same window as the default allowance.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued and cannot be asked for per call.\"},{\"text\":\"The tier cannot be asked for per call.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued and cannot be asked for per call.\"},{\"text\":\"Nothing else differs between the default and batch tiers.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\"},{\"text\":\"The log line for a refusal should carry the credential, the window and the wait.\",\"line\":25,\"span\":\"The log line should carry the credential, the window and the wait.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons besides the cap.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons and only one of them is the one above.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons, only one of which is the cap.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons and only one of them is the one above.\"},{\"text\":\"A credential may be suspended.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\"},{\"text\":\"A route may be closed for maintenance.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\"},{\"text\":\"The request body limit is 5 megabyte.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\"},{\"text\":\"None of the three non-cap refusal conditions (suspended credential, route closed for maintenance, body over the 5 megabyte limit) clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds.\"},{\"text\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service.\",\"line\":31,\"span\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service — and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\"},{\"text\":\"Reading the status code rather than its class costs one comparison.\",\"line\":31,\"span\":\"Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to is what separates the two cases, and it costs one comparison.\"},{\"text\":\"A cap can be raised.\",\"line\":35,\"span\":\"A cap can be raised, and the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0.\"},{\"text\":\"The number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0.\",\"line\":35,\"span\":\"A cap can be raised, and the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0.\"},{\"text\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty when considering a cap increase.\",\"line\":35,\"span\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty — a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\"},{\"text\":\"A burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\",\"line\":35,\"span\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty — a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\"},{\"text\":\"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap.\",\"line\":35,\"span\":\"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all, which is the outcome everyone prefers.\"},{\"text\":\"Cap increase requests reach the platform team through the usual channel.\",\"line\":37,\"span\":\"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel, and they are answered within two working days.\"},{\"text\":\"Cap increase requests are answered within two working days.\",\"line\":37,\"span\":\"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel, and they are answered within two working days.\"},{\"text\":\"There is no expedited path for cap increase requests.\",\"line\":37,\"span\":\"There is no expedited path and no exception list.\"},{\"text\":\"There is no exception list for cap increase requests.\",\"line\":37,\"span\":\"There is no expedited path and no exception list.\"}]}","ttft_ms":24617,"type":"result","duration_ms":24636,"uuid":"f6d14e72-5a74-496e-b71a-1479fcdf45d2","ttft_stream_ms":1473,"time_to_request_ms":91,"first_content_frame_ms":1474,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
